  "body": "Found in the second read of PR #3487 (head e30244c56). It is not a regression of that PR: the case needs a part hull less than about 1e-6 mm wide.\n\n## What happens\n`exterior::bound` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_exterior.rs:13-31`) returns `Some` also when `Region::new` normalizes the hull to an empty region. Then `clear_of` (`contour_depth.rs:124-135`) returns true and the edge loop has no edge to check. Each ring is \"clear of the part\", and the depth ladder is skipped.\n\nThe check fails open. A check of this kind must fail closed.\n\n## Wanted\n- `bound` returns `None` when the normalized region is empty, so that the section checks run.\n- Unit tests for `exterior::clear`: a ring inside the hull, a ring that crosses it, a ring at `need - epsilon`, a ring that encloses it, and the empty hull.\n\nThe work is under the safety floor (a gouge check).\n",
